---
// No layout needed for pure technical test
---

<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="utf-8" />
        <title>Inti.js UnoCSS Engine Test</title>
    </head>
    <body>
        <main class="min-h-screen bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-8 font-sans">
            <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6">
                <header class="border-b border-slate-700 pb-4">
                    <h1
                        class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-sky-400 to-indigo-500"
                    >
                        Inti.js Adaptive Styling
                    </h1>
                    <p class="mt-2 text-slate-400">
                        If you see these Tailwind styles applied, <span
                            class="text-emerald-400 font-semibold"
                            >UnoCSS + Preset Wind</span
                        > is working perfectly in the "Core Engine".
                    </p>
                </header>

                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                    <div
                        class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-slate-800 border border-slate-700 shadow-lg hover:shadow-sky-500/20 transition-all duration-300"
                    >
                        <div
                            class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-sky-500/20 flex items-center justify-center mb-4 text-sky-400"
                        >
                            <svg
                                class="w-6 h-6"
                                fill="none"
                                stroke="currentColor"
                                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                                ><path
                                    stroke-linecap="round"
                                    stroke-linejoin="round"
                                    stroke-width="2"
                                    d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"></path></svg
                            >
                        </div>
                        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">
                            Extreme Speed
                        </h2>
                        <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
                            UnoCSS generates classes on demand and injects them into
                            Astro SSR immediately, with no build latency from
                            heavy Webpack or Vite.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div
                        class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-slate-800 border border-slate-700 shadow-lg hover:shadow-indigo-500/20 transition-all duration-300"
                    >
                        <div
                            class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-indigo-500/20 flex items-center justify-center mb-4 text-indigo-400"
                        >
                            <svg
                                class="w-6 h-6"
                                fill="none"
                                stroke="currentColor"
                                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                                ><path
                                    stroke-linecap="round"
                                    stroke-linejoin="round"
                                    stroke-width="2"
                                    d="M9 12l2 2 4-4M7.835 4.697a3.42 3.42 0 001.946-.806 3.42 3.42 0 014.438 0 3.42 3.42 0 001.946.806 3.42 3.42 0 013.138 3.138 3.42 3.42 0 00.806 1.946 3.42 3.42 0 010 4.438 3.42 3.42 0 00-.806 1.946 3.42 3.42 0 01-3.138 3.138 3.42 3.42 0 00-1.946.806 3.42 3.42 0 01-4.438 0 3.42 3.42 0 00-1.946-.806 3.42 3.42 0 01-3.138-3.138 3.42 3.42 0 00-.806-1.946 3.42 3.42 0 010-4.438 3.42 3.42 0 00.806-1.946 3.42 3.42 0 013.138-3.138z"
                                ></path></svg
                            >
                        </div>
                        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">
                            Smart Detection
                        </h2>
                        <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
                            If a user plugin or theme includes Tailwind
                            CSS, this framework gracefully disables this
                            component and logs a warning (fallback
                            hybrid setup).
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </main>
    </body>
</html>
